{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02000","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02000@rel:R25-11#a8ba80b5","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02000","release":"R25-11","content":"enumeration ExecutionState [SWS_EM_02000] Upstream: RS_EM_00103 , RS_AP_00125 , RS_AP_00143 , RS_AP_00129 enum class ExecutionState : std::uint32_t {...}; Defines the internal states of a Process. Scoped enumeration of uint32_t. Please note that ara::exec::ExecutionState includes only states reportable by the Process to Execution Management and therefore does not include enumerations e.g. the \"Initializing\" state mentioned in Figure 7.2 and Figure 7.12, which are an implied states for Execution Management. The Initializing state starts when Process is first scheduled (so no code executed yet) and ends when kRunning is reported ( [SWS_EM_01004] ). The Terminating state starts when termination is requested by Execution Management and ends when the Process terminates ( [SWS_EM_01404] ). For the reasons mentioned, Execution Management assumes that Process is in initializing state until kRunning will be reported by it. Header-Datei #include \"ara/exec/execution_client.h\" class mono Forwarding-Header #include \"ara/exec/exec_fwd.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::exec class mono Symbol ExecutionState class mono Basistyp std::uint32_t class mono Werte th Enumerator th Beschreibung td kRunning td =0 After a Process has been started by Execution Management, it reports ExecutionState kRunning.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"242e5dc2ef4f"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02000","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_re